The problem may be in the batch file that ships with Hearse; it's only 
set to run the TTY version of NetHack. You can modify it to run the 
tiled version (just open it in any text editor); it should contain a 
line like:

  start /w nethack %1 %2 %3 %4 %5 %6 %7 %8 %9

You can change the "nethack" part to "nethackw" (or whichever 
executable runs the tiled version), and it'll run the tiled NetHack.


As an aside, is there any special reason you're running 3.4.1, as 
opposed to 3.4.3? No biggie or anything, just curious.


